    // ── Embedded terminal (terminal/) ─────────────────────────────────
    // Context keys are set by terminal/commands.py; keys stay inert in
    // ordinary views. Terminal views also pin super+w to close,
    // handing the live pty back instead of orphaning it.
    //
    // ctrl+/ opens the terminal. Not cmd+/ — that is Sublime's toggle
    // comment. The tag (also the tab title) makes a repeat press focus the
    // same terminal instead of stacking sheets; the palette entry stays
    // tag-free so extra terminals are still one command away.
    {
        "keys": ["ctrl+/"],
        "command": "submarine_terminal_open",
        "args": {
            "tag": "Terminal",
            "cwd": "${file_path:${folder}}"
        }
    },
    // ── The no-session page (ui/idle.py) ────────────────────────────────
